  fishName: Tyrantworm
  description: The Tyrantworm is a huge, slow-moving ambush-predator. It's hunting
    tactics are simple- simply lie in wait with its lure hanging in front of its
    mouth and wait. On Nimbus, where most things use some form of bioluminescence
    to hunt, see, or attract a mate, the tyrantworm never has trouble attracting
    curious prey.\n\n  Chef's Notes:\n How huge! Unlike the Wale, this one only has
    quantity on its size. Its meat is... voluminous. It's certainly... expansive.
    What on earth am I going to do with all this...
